  panel.innerHTML = "<div class=\"op-wrap\"><header class=\"op-hero\"><span class=\"op-kicker\">What we would build to get there</span><h3>The product this opportunity rests on</h3><p>The capabilities above are a hypothesis about what the system could become. This is what six people independently said the product should do &mdash; read against the loops, the overlap is much larger than the disagreement.</p></header><div class=\"op-subnav\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Choose a product view\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn-primary\" data-op-panel=\"converged\" aria-pressed=\"true\">Where we converged</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"btn\" data-op-panel=\"authors\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Every definition, by author</button></div><div class=\"op-panel\" data-op-body=\"converged\"><div class=\"op-grid\"><article class=\"op-card\"><div class=\"op-head\"><span class=\"op-count\">5 of 6</span><span class=\"op-strength\">converged</span></div><h4>Members must see earned, pending, redeemed and missing value</h4><p>Five of six, described independently in near-identical state language - including the same insistence that missing or unresolved value be visible, not only successful value.</p><p class=\"op-why\">The most defensible product capability in the set. Five people would build it and none treat it as optional. It is phase 1.</p><div class=\"op-drawn\"><span class=\"op-who\">Sly</span><span class=\"op-who\">Josh</span><span class=\"op-who\">Joann</span><span class=\"op-who\">Henry</span><span class=\"op-who\">Ola</span></div></article><article class=\"op-card\"><div class=\"op-head\"><span class=\"op-count\">5 of 6</span><span class=\"op-strength\">converged</span></div><h4>Surface worthwhile, relevant opportunities the member can act on</h4><p>Five of six include relevance-driven opportunity surfacing as a member-facing capability.</p><p class=\"op-diff\"><strong>What differs.</strong> The qualifier differs and it matters. Sly and Henry qualify relevance by what the member already intends to buy - inferable from behaviour. Josh qualifies it by a goal the member has stated - which requires member input and consent first.</p><p class=\"op-why\">The qualifier sets the data dependency, and therefore whether this can ship before or after goal capture.</p><div class=\"op-drawn\"><span class=\"op-who\">Sly</span><span class=\"op-who\">Josh</span><span class=\"op-who\">Henry</span><span class=\"op-who\">Lia</span><span class=\"op-who\">Joann</span></div></article><article class=\"op-card\"><div class=\"op-head\"><span class=\"op-count\">4 of 6</span><span class=\"op-strength\">converged</span></div><h4>Same channel assumption: embedded, not a new destination</h4><p>Four of six independently assume an embedded experience in existing authenticated channels, and all four explicitly decline to replace the underlying loyalty, banking or partner systems. Nobody proposed a standalone app.</p><p class=\"op-why\">Removes a whole class of architectural argument from the team's remaining decisions.</p><div class=\"op-drawn\"><span class=\"op-who\">Sly</span><span class=\"op-who\">Josh</span><span class=\"op-who\">Henry</span><span class=\"op-who\">Joann</span></div></article><article class=\"op-card is-partial\"><div class=\"op-head\"><span class=\"op-count\">3 of 6</span><span class=\"op-strength\">partial</span></div><h4>Member-stated goals as the organizing unit of value</h4><p>Three contributors organise the system around something other than a points balance. Two build it around a goal the member states; the third around whether promised value was delivered.</p><p class=\"op-diff\"><strong>What differs.</strong> Joann treats the goal as the unit of value but keeps realized value as the measurable proxy. Josh treats goal achievement as the system's organizing objective outright. Sly organises around realized value and has no member-stated goal construct \u2014 his objective is measurable from system events without asking the member anything, which is the argument that settled DV-01.</p><p class=\"op-why\">This is the concrete product consequence of DV-01. The settlement nests them: realized value is the main variable and the measurable proxy, member goal achievement is the ultimate goal it serves. Goal capture is therefore phase 3, not phase 1 \u2014 the system has to work for members who never set a goal.</p><div class=\"op-drawn\"><span class=\"op-who\">Josh</span><span class=\"op-who\">Joann</span><span class=\"op-who\">Sly</span></div></article></div></div><div class=\"op-panel\" data-op-body=\"authors\" hidden><p class=\"op-lead\">Each contributor's product definition as they wrote it, before merging. The merged themes sit under Where we converged.</p><div class=\"op-authors\"><article class=\"op-author\"><div class=\"op-author-head\"><h4>Joann</h4><span class=\"op-src\">Initial Product Description</span></div><p class=\"op-one\">A goal-linked rewards layer for BMO Blue Rewards that turns a points balance into visible progress toward something the member is actually trying to achieve, and can measure.</p><ul class=\"op-caps\"><li class=\"\"><strong>Declare a goal, and set its terms</strong><p>State a financial or reward goal, the preferences that shape what counts as a good opportunity, and the data permissions that fund the personalization.</p></li><li class=\"\"><strong>See what a choice is worth before making it</strong><p>Compare how a spending, saving, payment or redemption decision moves them toward the goal \u2014 in dollars against the goal rather than points against nothing.</p></li><li class=\"\"><strong>Receive opportunities that are legible as help</strong><p>Timely, goal-linked offers that state why this member is seeing this offer now and what it advances, so relevance is demonstrated rather than asserted.</p></li><li class=\"is-wedge\"><strong>Track what they have and what's missing</strong><span class=\"op-wedge\">starts here</span><p>Progress toward the goal, plus a reliable ledger of earned, pending, redeemed and missing rewards, with a path to resolve the missing ones.</p></li></ul><div class=\"op-row\"><span>Who it is for</span><p>BMO customers and rewards-only members who are earning value they don't fully see, don't accurately price, and don't reliably collect.</p></div><div class=\"op-row\"><span>The job</span><p>Tell me what I've actually got, what it's worth, and what it would take to get where I'm going.</p></div><div class=\"op-row\"><span>What is distinctive</span><p>Takes a position it says should be tested: value members actually collect and understand is worth more over time than value they forfeit. Treats permission as an exchange rather than a gate \u2014 personalization intensity that outruns demonstrated value degrades the signal supply it depends on.</p></div><div class=\"op-row\"><span>Out of scope</span><p>Not a new points currency, not a standalone app, and not a replacement for offer economics, payment rails or reward issuance.</p></div></article><article class=\"op-author\"><div class=\"op-author-head\"><h4>Sylvester</h4><span class=\"op-src\">Published V1 site</span></div><p class=\"op-one\">A digital rewards experience that helps loyalty-program members discover worthwhile opportunities, see where promised value stands, and initiate or approve recovery when it is delayed, missing, or at risk.</p><ul class=\"op-caps\"><li class=\"\"><strong>Discover</strong><p>Surface worthwhile, attainable reward opportunities that a member can understand and act upon.</p></li><li class=\"\"><strong>Track</strong><p>Make qualification, earning, posting, redemption, fulfilment, and unresolved states visible.</p></li><li class=\"is-wedge\"><strong>Assure and recover</strong><span class=\"op-wedge\">starts here</span><p>Detect at-risk value, intervene or route it, and verify that promised value was realized.</p></li><li class=\"\"><strong>Learn</strong><p>Use realized, failed, and recovered outcomes to improve future decisions and system performance.</p></li></ul><div class=\"op-row\"><span>Who it is for</span><p>Loyalty-program members with worthwhile, eligible reward value already in motion and a detectable risk that some of it may be delayed, missed, or lost because of a qualification, posting, redemption, fulfilment, partner, or service breakdown.</p></div><div class=\"op-row\"><span>The job</span><p>Help me receive and use the worthwhile reward value I was promised\u2014and recover it without diagnosing the system or repeatedly chasing support when something breaks.</p></div><div class=\"op-row\"><span>What is distinctive</span><p>Names a product wedge outright: Proactive Value Assurance and Recovery. Monitor worthwhile reward opportunities as they progress from qualification through earning, redemption, and fulfilment; identify when promised value is delayed, missing, or at risk; and either resolve the issue automatically or route it to the responsible service pathway with the necessary context. Members remain informed and retain approval over consequential actions, while recovery outcomes help identify and prevent recurring sources of value loss.</p></div><div class=\"op-row\"><span>Out of scope</span><p>Replacing loyalty, banking, partner, or service systems; maximizing redemption at any cost; treating intentional saving or informed rejection as value loss; forcing banking conversion; or masking structural failures through repeated case-by-case recovery.</p></div></article><article class=\"op-author\"><div class=\"op-author-head\"><h4>Henry</h4><span class=\"op-src\">Henry \u2014 product definition</span></div><p class=\"op-one\">A personalized rewards value experience embedded within existing BMO and Blue Rewards digital channels that helps members discover relevant earning and redemption opportunities tied to spending they already intend to do, understand and compare reward value, requirements and trade-offs, track the value they have earned, and resolve missing or unclear rewards.</p><ul class=\"op-caps\"><li class=\"\"><strong>Discover relevant opportunities</strong><p>Tied to spending they already intend to do.</p></li><li class=\"\"><strong>Understand and compare</strong><p>Reward value, requirements and trade-offs made comparable.</p></li><li class=\"\"><strong>Track earned value</strong><p>Follow what has been earned.</p></li><li class=\"\"><strong>Resolve missing or unclear rewards</strong><p>Close the gap when value does not arrive or cannot be understood.</p></li></ul><div class=\"op-row\"><span>Who it is for</span><p>Members who want to realize more worthwhile value with less effort and uncertainty.</p></div><div class=\"op-row\"><span>The job</span><p>Help me get more of the value I am owed without the effort and uncertainty.</p></div><div class=\"op-row\"><span>What is distinctive</span><p>The only definition that spans discovery, comparison, tracking and resolution without naming a starting point.</p></div></article><article class=\"op-author\"><div class=\"op-author-head\"><h4>Josh</h4><span class=\"op-src\">Milestone 2 document</span></div><p class=\"op-one\">An integrated digital rewards experience that surfaces relevant rewards, partner experiences and appropriate BMO products and services at the moment they can best help members achieve their goals.</p><ul class=\"op-caps\"><li class=\"\"><strong>Set goals and permissions</strong><p>Set custom financial and reward goals, preferences and data permissions.</p></li><li class=\"\"><strong>Compare choices against goals</strong><p>Compare how spending, saving, payment and redemption choices could help them achieve their goals.</p></li><li class=\"is-wedge\"><strong>Receive goal-linked opportunities</strong><span class=\"op-wedge\">starts here</span><p>Receive timely, goal-linked opportunities and incentives.</p></li><li class=\"\"><strong>Track progress and rewards</strong><p>Easily track goal progress as well as earned, pending, redeemed or missing rewards.</p></li></ul><div class=\"op-row\"><span>Who it is for</span><p>BMO customers and rewards-only members who want valuable opportunities without searching across channels, calculating reward value or chasing missing rewards.</p></div><div class=\"op-row\"><span>The job</span><p>Help me align my spending, saving, payment and reward choices with the goals I actually have \u2014 without hunting across channels or doing the math myself.</p></div><div class=\"op-row\"><span>What is distinctive</span><p>The product uses visible progress, timely feedback and well-designed incentives to help members align their spending, saving, payment and reward choices with their goals.</p></div><div class=\"op-row\"><span>Out of scope</span><p>BMO and partners retain responsibility for offer economics, payments and reward issuance.</p></div></article><article class=\"op-author\"><div class=\"op-author-head\"><h4>Lia</h4><span class=\"op-src\">Two Connected Loops diagram; 5 Sept session</span></div><p class=\"op-one\">Make Blue Rewards easier and more relevant to use, while still giving members control.</p><ul class=\"op-caps\"><li class=\"is-wedge\"><strong>More relevant offers</strong><span class=\"op-wedge\">starts here</span><p>Use the behavioural insight the programme already has to fit offers to everyday spending.</p></li><li class=\"\"><strong>Member control over data</strong><p>Keep the member clear about, and in control of, how their data is used.</p></li></ul><div class=\"op-row\"><span>Who it is for</span><p>Members whose everyday spending should be producing more relevant offers than it does.</p></div><div class=\"op-row\"><span>The job</span><p>Show me offers that actually fit how I spend, without making me feel watched.</p></div><div class=\"op-row\"><span>What is distinctive</span><p>The shortest definition in the set, and the only one that makes control a headline rather than a caveat.</p></div></article><article class=\"op-author\"><div class=\"op-author-head\"><h4>Ola</h4><span class=\"op-src\">System Loops PDF, page 3</span></div><p class=\"op-one\">A connected capability inside Blue Rewards, surfaced contextually in BMO's banking app, that shows members relevant earning and redemption opportunities matched to spending they are already doing, gives them a clear standardised view of what they have earned and what it is worth, and detects and helps resolve value that did not show up as promised.</p><ul class=\"op-caps\"><li class=\"\"><strong>Surface relevant opportunities</strong><p>Earning and redemption opportunities matched to spending the member is already doing.</p></li><li class=\"\"><strong>A standardised view of earned value</strong><p>Clear and consistent: what has been earned, and what it is worth.</p></li><li class=\"\"><strong>Detect and resolve missing value</strong><p>Find value that did not show up as promised, and help resolve it.</p></li></ul><div class=\"op-row\"><span>Who it is for</span><p>Every member \u2014 the definition is explicit that it does these three things for every member.</p></div><div class=\"op-row\"><span>The job</span><p>Show me what I can get, what I've got and what it's worth, and fix it when it doesn't arrive.</p></div><div class=\"op-row\"><span>What is distinctive</span><p>Names the product \u2014 The Value Hub \u2014 and places it contextually inside the banking app rather than in the loyalty programme alone. The only definition that treats all three capabilities as a single connected thing rather than a sequence.</p></div></article></div></div><p class=\"op-fine\">Each capability above is governed by a balancing loop the team found independently: permissioned identity by trust and consent, coordinated delivery by the value gap, net relationship value by programme economics. Select a capability to see which.</p></div>";
  var legend = root.querySelector(":scope > .lm2-legend");
